sequenceDiagram
accTitle: A NAT idle timeout breaks a reused TCP connection
accDescr: A connection that is idle beyond 350 seconds expires and receives a reset on reuse. Keepalive traffic before the timeout prevents expiration from inactivity.
participant C as Private EC2 client
participant N as NAT gateway
participant S as External service
C->>N: TCP application request
N->>S: Forward request
S-->>C: Response through NAT
alt No traffic for more than 350 seconds
Note over N: Idle connection expires
C->>N: Reuse old connection
N-->>C: TCP RST
else Keepalive starts before 350 seconds
C->>N: TCP keepalive probe
N->>S: Forward probe
S-->>C: Response through NAT
Note over C,S: Connection remains active while probes continue
end
